[f1ff07cb] 2026-10-25T08:40:40.356Z: US state names don't always match their fips codes, e.g. 'Washington' in DC and MD, 'Washington County' in IN and PA. Zero-pad fips codes to 5 chars when matching.
[e678f22e] 2026-10-25T07:50:40.459Z: When listing state capitals, be sure to strip non-alphanumeric from state names before matching, or you'll miss some. Just had to debug this for the 5th time.
[c0abd0be] 2026-10-06T13:50:28.891Z: Washington County has multiple FIPS codes, state_fips + county_fips is key, not state_fips alone. Tested in 3 runs, confirmed works.